From: Kettle Linux <noreply@kettlelinux>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250: A650 overclock OPPs to 750 MHz

The bottom of the frequency ladder from ROCKNIX's SM8250
9998-gpu-tuning (KonaBess steps): 650 and 670 MHz at NOM_L1 (670
opened to speed bin 0, the base SD865), 700 MHz at TURBO, 725 and
750 MHz at TURBO_L1, each with the 587 MHz bandwidth vote from 0110.

ROCKNIX goes on to 925 MHz. On an RP5 (with ACD, 0112) 750 MHz ran
Cleared Hot about 11% faster than 587 MHz with the GPU at 80 C and no
GPU errors; 800 MHz added almost nothing at 82 C, near the 85 C passive
trip, with the fan already at full speed.

kettle-powerd keeps auto at the stock 587 MHz (rp5.toml auto_max_mhz):
these clocks are only for a manual GPU clock, which Steam keeps per
game.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250.dtsi
@@ -2976,10 +2976,38 @@
 			gpu_opp_table: opp-table {
 				compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
+				opp-750000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <750000000>;
+					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO_L1>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+				};
+
+				opp-725000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <725000000>;
+					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO_L1>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+				};
+
+				opp-700000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <700000000>;
+					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_TURBO>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+				};
+
 				opp-670000000 {
 					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <670000000>;
 					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM_L1>;
-					opp-supported-hw = <0xa>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
+				};
+
+				opp-650000000 {
+					opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <650000000>;
+					opp-level = <RPMH_REGULATOR_LEVEL_NOM_L1>;
+					opp-supported-hw = <0xb>;
 					opp-peak-kBps = <8171875>;
 				};
 
